Id: cont008w
Severity: WARN
Category: containers
Check: check_containers
Fix: Mount only the files the container needs, read-only (:ro).
References: docker-run(1) --volume
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-6, CM-7; ISO 8.2, 8.9; CE Secure configuration, User access control

A running container has the host's / or /etc mounted, writable. It can
then change the host's configuration: add a user, a sudoers rule, a
cron job or a systemd unit, and so run what it likes on the host as
root.

To fix it, mount only the files the container needs, and read-only
(:ro), or copy the configuration it needs into its image.
